  "$rings": "In the Making's rings, in the order the page shows them, top to bottom. Each one turns as the page scrolls. `centre` is the still picture in the middle: `{\"release\": \"<id>\"}` reuses a release's cover and alt text, `{\"src\": \"<path>\"}` is a picture of its own (its alt text is `centreAlt` in the locale files), and a ring with neither has a hole in the middle. `photos` go round it in this order; a photo's words live under its id in the locale files, and one with a description - or `opens` set - can be clicked open. Three optional keys set the geometry, and each one left out uses the stylesheet's own value: `tilt` and `lean` in degrees, and `dir` (1 for clockwise as the page scrolls, -1 for the other way). The admin's In the Making tab has sliders for them.",
